<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-16"?>
<!--
  Task definition for "clientname" on TX-PW0FNXY8.

  Register with:
      schtasks /create /tn clientname /xml rdp2tcp-task.xml /f

  The task used to be logon-triggered only, which is why rdp2tcp did not come
  back after a reconnect on 2026-10-02. Reconnecting re-attaches to a session
  that already exists (LocalSessionManager event 25), rather than creating a new
  one (event 21), so a logon trigger never fires.

  The triggers cover every way the helper can be missing:

    LogonTrigger          a fresh session, event 21
    RemoteConnect         a reconnect into an existing session, event 25
    TimeTrigger           everything else, in particular a crash mid-session,
                          which no session event reports at all

  The repetition is what makes this self-correcting rather than a list of cases
  someone has to keep complete. Five minutes is chosen against the cost of being
  wrong: the guard is a short-lived PowerShell process that most of the time
  looks for a process, finds it, and exits.

  The recurring check is a TimeTrigger rather than a Repetition on the logon
  trigger, and the difference is not cosmetic. Repetition on a logon trigger
  only arms once a logon has happened, so a task registered at 13:38 reports
  Next Run Time: N/A and would not check anything until the next time someone
  logged in, precisely the window where a crashed helper would go unnoticed.
  A TimeTrigger with a start boundary in the past is armed from the moment it is
  registered.

  The guard also refuses to do anything when it is not in a real interactive
  session, since a TimeTrigger fires whether or not anyone is logged in. Without
  that check it would start a useless copy in session 0, which has no virtual
  channel to attach to.

  Runs as the user with InteractiveToken, which is what puts it in the
  interactive session, the only one whose virtual channel means anything.

  IgnoreNew and a two minute execution limit go together. Two guards must never
  run at once, so the second is dropped rather than queued, but IgnoreNew alone
  turns a single hung guard into a task that is silently dead from then on. The
  limit bounds that: the guard normally exits in well under a second, so two
  minutes is a hundredfold margin, and AllowHardTerminate lets the scheduler
  actually enforce it rather than asking a console process to stop itself.
  Windows releases a process's mutex when it dies, so a terminated guard cannot
  leave the next one wedged on the lock.

  DisallowStartIfOnBatteries and StopIfGoingOnBatteries are off. This is a
  laptop and both default to true; leaving them on would mean the helper quietly
  never starts when the machine is unplugged, which is the same class of silent
  failure this file exists to fix.

  Note that XML comments may not contain two consecutive hyphens, which is why
  the above avoids them.
-->
<Task version="1.2" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Date>2023-08-01T10:27:53.1437866</Date>
    <Author>10_0_24_7\Administrator</Author>
    <Description>Keep the rdp2tcp virtual-channel helper running in the interactive session.</Description>
    <URI>\clientname</URI>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <UserId>S-1-5-21-4198808933-4151079717-884742619-500</UserId>
      <LogonType>InteractiveToken</LogonType>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  <Settings>
    <AllowHardTerminate>true</AllowHardTerminate>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>false</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>false</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>PT2M</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <IdleSettings>
      <StopOnIdleEnd>false</StopOnIdleEnd>
      <RestartOnIdle>false</RestartOnIdle>
    </IdleSettings>
    <StartWhenAvailable>true</StartWhenAvailable>
  </Settings>
  <Triggers>
    <LogonTrigger>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    </LogonTrigger>
    <SessionStateChangeTrigger>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <StateChange>RemoteConnect</StateChange>
      <Delay>PT5S</Delay>
      <UserId>S-1-5-21-4198808933-4151079717-884742619-500</UserId>
    </SessionStateChangeTrigger>
    <TimeTrigger>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <StartBoundary>2026-10-02T00:00:00</StartBoundary>
      <Repetition>
        <Interval>PT5M</Interval>
        <StopAtDurationEnd>false</StopAtDurationEnd>
      </Repetition>
    </TimeTrigger>
  </Triggers>
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>powershell.exe</Command>
      <Arguments>-NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -WindowStyle Hidden -File "C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\rdp2tcp-launch.ps1"</Arguments>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
</Task>
